# No environment variables are required yet — this is a static, client-only React app (see
# CLAUDE.md §1/§2). This file exists so the prefix rule below is on record before the Contact
# app (Phase 1) needs its first real variable.
#
# Vite only exposes vars prefixed with VITE_ to the client bundle — anyone can read them in the
# shipped JS. Never put a real secret behind that prefix. A non-prefixed var is invisible to
# import.meta.env in the browser; a future backend needing real secrets must handle them outside
# this repo (e.g. in the hosting platform's own env config), never here.
